---
import {
  AiChat02Icon,
  Analytics01Icon,
  Key01Icon,
  SearchList01Icon,
} from '@hugeicons/core-free-icons'
import CodeBlock from '@/components/CodeBlock.astro'
import FeaturePage from '@/components/FeaturePage.astro'

const related = [
  { title: 'seo research', text: 'The AI answer check, its options and how to run it from the CLI.', href: '/docs/research', icon: SearchList01Icon },
  { title: 'API keys', text: 'Add a DataForSEO key to the hosted MCP or the CLI.', href: '/docs/keys', icon: Key01Icon },
  { title: 'SEO report', text: 'The AI queries section and visits from AI assistants.', href: '/docs/report', icon: Analytics01Icon },
  { title: 'AI search tracking', text: 'Every way SEO Skill reads AI search, from questions to crawlers.', href: '/features/ai-search', icon: AiChat02Icon, link: 'AI search tracking' },
]
---

<FeaturePage
  title="AI visibility checker"
  metaTitle="AI visibility checker for ChatGPT, AI Mode and AI Overviews"
  description="Check whether ChatGPT search, Google AI Mode and AI Overviews cite or mention your site for up to 10 questions, and which sites they cite instead."
  path="/features/ai-visibility-checker"
  lead="Ask your agent whether ChatGPT search, Google AI Mode and Google AI Overviews cite your site for the questions people already ask, and which sites they cite instead."
  {related}
  relatedHeading="Read more"
>
  <h2>What the AI visibility checker returns for each question</h2>
  <p>
    The AI visibility checker in SEO Skill asks up to 10 questions on
    ChatGPT search, Google AI Mode and Google AI Overviews, so one check is
    up to 30 answers. Each answer gets one of four results:
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Result</th><th>What it means</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Cited</td><td>The answer lists or links a page on your site.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Mentioned</td><td>The answer names your site or brand in its text, with no link.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Neither</td><td>The answer gave no link to your site and did not name it.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>No AI answer</td><td>The engine showed no AI answer for that question.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    Every answer also lists the other sites it cites, and the result ranks
    the sites cited most across the whole check. Those are the pages the AI
    used instead of yours, so open them first to see what they cover.
  </p>
  <p>
    A check of 10 questions costs about 7 cents of DataForSEO credit, and
    most answers come back in about 15 seconds. It runs when you ask. SEO
    Skill does not run it on a schedule or store a history of past checks.
  </p>

  <h2>Set up the checker in 3 steps</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      Add the hosted MCP server to Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, ChatGPT or any
      client with remote MCP, and sign in with Google. The commands are at
      the top of this page.
    </li>
    <li>
      Save a <a href="/docs/keys">DataForSEO key</a> on your account page.
      DataForSEO bills you directly for each check, and SEO Skill adds
      nothing on top. The AI answer check needs DataForSEO; an Ahrefs key
      does not run it.
    </li>
    <li>Ask your agent, like the prompts below.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Prefer a terminal? <code>npm i -g seo</code> then <code>seo start</code>{' '}
    sets up the CLI, and <code>seo providers dataforseo connect</code> keeps
    the key on your machine.
  </p>

  <h2>Check the questions people already ask AI about your site</h2>
  <p>
    The most useful questions to check are ones real people ask. When people
    use Google's AI Mode, or an AI assistant searches the web for them, their
    questions show up in your Search Console as long, chat-style queries. With
    Google connected, ask:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock value={`Check whether AI answers cite example.com for the questions people ask about it`} wrap />
  <p>
    The checker takes the top 10 chat-style and long questions from the last
    90 days of your Search Console, and shows each one's impressions beside
    its answers. A "neither" on a question with 400 impressions matters more
    than one on a question with 3. In a terminal:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock value={`seo research ai_answers --target example.com --country us`} wrap />

  <h2>Check your own questions on any site, including a competitor's</h2>
  <p>
    To check prompts you choose, give up to 10 questions. The target can then
    be any site, and Google does not need to be connected:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock value={`Ask ChatGPT, AI Mode and AI Overviews "what is the best crm for a small team" and "how do I import contacts into a crm", and check whether they cite competitor.example`} wrap />
  <CodeBlock value={`seo research ai_answers --target competitor.example --keywords "what is the best crm for a small team,how do I import contacts into a crm"`} wrap />
  <p>
    Run the same questions for your site and a competitor's, and the
    difference is the list of answers where they get cited and you don't.
  </p>

  <h2>Count every domain and brand name you use</h2>
  <p>
    The checker counts a mention when the answer names your site, taken from
    the domain unless you say otherwise. When your brand name differs from
    your domain, or you run more than one domain, tell it:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock value={`seo research ai_answers --target example.com --also example.org --brand "Example" --keywords "what is example"`} wrap />
  <p>
    A citation to any of the domains counts as cited. Placeholder sites in an
    answer, such as yourdomain.com, and images in ChatGPT's answers never
    count as citations.
  </p>

  <h2>Check AI Overviews for your keywords</h2>
  <p>
    Every check already asks Google AI Overviews each question. For
    ordinary keywords, a SERP request is a quick AI Overview checker: for up
    to 5 keywords it says whether Google showed an AI Overview, lists the
    sites it cited, and shows the ranking pages underneath.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock value={`Show the top 10 for "free ai visibility checker" and the sites its AI Overview cites`} wrap />
  <p>
    Each ranking page comes with Domain Rating by{' '}
    <a href="https://ahrefs.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Ahrefs</a>,
    free on the hosted MCP. When we ran that request for the US on 11
    November 2026, Google showed an AI Overview for "free ai visibility
    checker" that cited 5 sites: ahrefs.com, amplitude.com, honeyb.ai,
    arobis.ai and seocrawl.ai. The small sites sit next to the big ones,
    which is a reason to check the AI Overview before you decide a keyword
    is out of reach.
  </p>

  <h2>A real check: AI answers named seoskill.dev in 4 of 30 answers</h2>
  <p>
    On 11 November 2026 we checked seoskill.dev in the US with 10 questions
    of our own, such as "what is the best google search console mcp server"
    and "how can I check if chatgpt cites my website". With "SEO Skill" as
    the brand, the 30 answers cost $0.072:
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Result</th><th>Answers (of 30)</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Cited</td><td>0</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Mentioned</td><td>4</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Neither</td><td>26</td></tr>
      <tr><td>No AI answer</td><td>0</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    Not one answer cited a page on seoskill.dev. The other sites cited most
    were github.com (in 12 answers), google.com (10), youtube.com (9),
    reddit.com (5) and ahrefs.com (4).
  </p>
  <p>
    Three of the 4 mentions came from one question, "is there an seo skill
    for claude code", where the brand name is also the words of the
    question. A mention is a text match, so when your brand is an everyday
    phrase, read the answer before you count it as a win. The fourth mention
    came from Google AI Mode for "how do I connect google search console to
    claude code", and it is the one we would open and read first.
  </p>

  <h2>Repeat a check to follow ChatGPT visibility over time</h2>
  <p>
    SEO Skill checks AI answers on demand. It is not a ChatGPT visibility
    tracker that stores daily history, and the paid weekly site audit does
    not ask AI answers. To follow the same questions over time, ask your
    agent to run the check again on the same site, country and questions,
    and compare the two results:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock value={`Run the AI answer check for example.com again with the same 10 questions as last month, and show which answers changed`} wrap />
  <p>
    In a terminal, add <code>--json</code> and save each run to a file. Once a
    month is often enough. Each answer is one sample, and the same question
    can get a different answer the next day, so one answer that flips is
    noise. A question that goes from cited on all 3 engines to none is a
    real change: open the pages the answers cite now.
  </p>

  <h2>See the visits AI assistants send you</h2>
  <p>
    Citations do not show whether anyone clicked. With Google Analytics
    connected, the <a href="/docs/report">SEO report</a> overview counts
    visits from ChatGPT, Perplexity, Claude, Gemini and Copilot by source,
    with the pages they land on:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock value={`Which AI assistants sent visits to example.com in the last 28 days, and which pages did they land on?`} wrap />
  <p>
    Only visits that pass a referrer count. An AI app that sends none shows
    up as Direct traffic, so treat the number as a minimum.
  </p>

  <h2>What one AI visibility check cannot prove</h2>
  <p>
    The checker asks ChatGPT search, Google AI Mode and Google AI Overviews.
    It does not ask Perplexity, Claude, Gemini or Copilot, although visits
    from them show in the report.
  </p>
  <p>
    Each answer is one sample from one country on one day, without a chat
    history. A "neither" is not proof the engine will never cite you, and a
    "cited" is not a ranking. For the questions themselves, the{' '}
    <a href="/features/ai-search">AI search tracking</a> page covers how
    SEO Skill finds the questions people ask AI in your Search Console.
  </p>
</FeaturePage>
